WEBVTT

00:33:57.864 --> 00:34:01.948
and so, yeah, I think he wanted to win,

00:34:01.972 --> 00:34:04.458
I think he wanted to win everything.

00:34:04.482 --> 00:34:06.388
AG: I've always bristled

00:34:06.412 --> 00:34:08.769
at the language of winning
and losing in business,

00:34:08.793 --> 00:34:13.580
because it's not like a soccer match,

00:34:13.604 --> 00:34:16.425
or a baseball game where there's a score

00:34:16.449 --> 00:34:18.252
and everybody has agreed on the rules

00:34:18.276 --> 00:34:21.790
and at the end of the game you know
what metric you are counting on.

00:34:22.186 --> 00:34:26.141
It seems like the moment
you define success in terms of winning,

00:34:26.165 --> 00:34:28.346
it means that everybody else has to lose.

00:34:29.295 --> 00:34:31.004
DF: Yeah, I totally agree with you,